# Settings persist to the per-project file <workspace>/.mnml/config.zon
# (the config is ZON; the Rust corpus asserted a TOML file here).
#
# Changing a setting in the overlay writes it to the workspace file at
# once, keystroke-driven end-to-end through the real key dispatcher. Esc
# restores the file's opened-state bytes, so the adjustment is undone on
# disk while a seeded value survives; Enter / click-outside keeps it.
write a.txt hello
open a.txt

# Seed an existing workspace config so Esc provably RESTORES it (not just
# deletes) and unrelated content survives a setting write.
write .mnml/config.zon .{\n    .ui = .{\n        .tree_width = 40,\n    },\n}\n

command view.settings
expect screen contains "Settings"

# Row 0 (first focusable) is `ui.line_numbers`. `→` adjusts it; the
# overlay writes the change live into the workspace file, beside the seed.
key right
expect file .mnml/config.zon contains ".line_numbers = false"
expect file .mnml/config.zon contains ".tree_width = 40"

# Esc cancels — the workspace file goes back to its pre-open bytes.
key esc
expect screen lacks "Settings"
expect file .mnml/config.zon lacks "line_numbers"
expect file .mnml/config.zon contains ".tree_width = 40"

# Reopen, adjust, and leave via click-outside (the keep path).
command view.settings
key right
click 1 1
expect screen lacks "Settings"
expect file .mnml/config.zon contains ".line_numbers = false"
